    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf5ce5f3_135f5712",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/dsp_comms/client/remote_lid_switch.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-03T18:57:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How does the initial state affect the lid angle calculation? After ISH FW is loaded, the ISH will request status from the EC which will include the lid switch state and so this value should be updated then.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "529d89873eaad4a050904b07bf662f01d0e5e975",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "db04061f_d8dea271",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/dsp_comms/client/remote_lid_switch.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380943
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-04T03:16:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @scott,\n\nTrulo devices has CBI DSP comms enabled hence we don\u0027t see this issue.\n\nThe initial value \"false\" indicates lid is closed. \nWe don\u0027t have a situation where the lid is in closed and the DUT boots to OS \u0026 ISH firmware is loaded. Hence i believe this is valid change.\n\nLet me know your thoughts.",
      "parentUuid": "cf5ce5f3_135f5712",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "529d89873eaad4a050904b07bf662f01d0e5e975",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d7271279_f86d045a",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/dsp_comms/client/remote_lid_switch.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T23:01:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This assumption (AP boot implies lid open) is not correct.  \n\nIf there is an external display connected, [depthcharge](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/depthcharge/src/vboot/ui/loop.c;l\u003d67;drc\u003d405bdcd9598750a9047a8f6140ae79b2571ced57) allows the kernel to boot, even if the lid is closed.",
      "parentUuid": "db04061f_d8dea271",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "529d89873eaad4a050904b07bf662f01d0e5e975",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ffe2444_18cff045",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/dsp_comms/client/remote_lid_switch.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T23:18:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I got further clarification from the AP firmware team.  depthcharge only performs the lid open check when the system is in developer or recovery mode.  During normal mode boot, depthcharge always boots into the kernel, allowing the kernel to make decisions about whether to remain powered up or not.",
      "parentUuid": "d7271279_f86d045a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "529d89873eaad4a050904b07bf662f01d0e5e975",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a5a499a_279c3188",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/dsp_comms/client/remote_lid_switch.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-06T00:05:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still don\u0027t think the initial value needs to be changed. I understand the point that it\u0027s a reasonable assumption the lid_switch is open when the ISH is initialized, but the source of truth is still the EC and it should suffice for the ISH to request the status as part of the ISH FW initialization.",
      "parentUuid": "db04061f_d8dea271",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "529d89873eaad4a050904b07bf662f01d0e5e975",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
